{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkdaR5kFQqwRyQwA7k2C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GQttpE2hWtpRpcwyo3JeK8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_3\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/heavy_tailed_signed_sensitivity_motif.py\necho coupled_switch_and_pattern_sensitivity > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `heavy_tailed_signed_sensitivity_motif` (people judge a sequence random to the extent their own second-order model of a fair coin explains it better than the regular generators they suspect — a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips — the evidence weighed per flip, with each person's own heavy-tailed, possibly reversed sensitivity and side habit). The single change is that a person's departure from the shared judgment is one trait, not two unrelated ones: how strongly (and in which direction) a person acts on the pattern evidence also carries over to their quick switch-count impression, so a person who is nearly indifferent to patterns is also nearly indifferent to switches, and a person who reverses the judgment (picking the sequence that looks less random) reverses their switch preference too, rather than keeping the majority's preference for more switching. This makes reversed and indifferent participants consistent across all pairs, including the short pairs that are decided mainly by switch count.\nEOF\npython - << EOF\nsrc = open(\"$SRC\").read()\ndoc_add = '''\"\"\"Coupled switch-impression and pattern sensitivity (one person-level trait).\n\nRefinement of `heavy_tailed_signed_sensitivity_motif`. Single change: the\nperson's switch-count weight w_i is no longer independent of their signed\npattern sensitivity beta_i = mu_b + sigma_b * z_beta_i; it loads on the same\nperson-level deviation, w_i = mu_w + kappa * sigma_b * z_beta_i + sigma_w * z_w_i\n(kappa fitted), so reversed or indifferent people are reversed/indifferent on\nthe switch impression too.\n\nDescription of the refined model follows.\n\n'''\nsrc = src.replace('\"\"\"', doc_add, 1)\nold = \"    w = mu_w + sigma_w * z_w\\n\"\nassert old in src\nsrc = src.replace(old, \"    # Coupling: the switch weight shares the person's sensitivity deviation.\\n    kappa = pm.Normal(\\\"kappa\\\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\\n    w = mu_w + kappa * sigma_b * z_beta + sigma_w * z_w\\n\")\nopen(\"$D/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nEOF\nhead -15 $D/candidate.py; grep -n \"kappa\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5338,"cache_read_input_tokens":82179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5338,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92a17996-fb10-41de-a780-ec3596d7f776","uuid":"b6804606-0b99-477f-bc81-6cfd70a8354a","timestamp":"2026-10-06T08:00:59.042Z","request_id":"req_011CfkdaQaUX3se5yWBr1rJp"}
